  "corridorNote": "Modelled on Room 32 at the National Gallery, London — the Julia and Hans Rausing Room: a wide, tall room with deep crimson walls, a continuous glazed lantern down the centre of the ceiling flanked by deeply coffered coves in red and gold, transverse gilded arches on a heavy gilded cornice, a light oak floor bordered in dark inlay, tufted leather seating down the centre, and an opening at the far end through to the next red room. A small number of very large works hang singly in heavy swept gilt frames.",
